\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid3679784\charrsid15034624 Awarded aid:}{\cf1\insrsid3679784\charrsid15034624  The dollar amounts offered to financial aid applicants.
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Financial aid applicant: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Any applicant who submits }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 any one of}{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 
 the institutionally required financial aid applications/forms, such as the FAFSA. 
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Indebtedness: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Aggregate dollar amount bo}{\cf1\insrsid1471844 rrowed through any loan program}{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 
 (federal, state, subsidized, unsubsidized, private, etc.; excluding parent loans) while the student was enrolled at an institution. Student loans co-signed by a parent are assumed to be the responsibility of the student and }{
\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 should}{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624  be included.
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1471844 {\b\cf1\highlight7\insrsid1471844\charrsid8486064 Institutional scholarships and grants}{\cf1\highlight7\insrsid1471844\charrsid8486064 
: Endowed scholarships, annual gifts and tuition funded grants for which the institution determines the recipient.}{\cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid75816 {\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Financial need: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 As determined by your institution using the federal methodology and/or your institution's own standards. 
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Need-based aid: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 College-funded or college-administered award from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must have financial need to qualify. This
 includes both institutional and noninstitutional student aid (grants, jobs, and loans).
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Need-based }{\b\cf1\insrsid1912817\charrsid15034624 scholarship or grant}{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624  aid: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 
Scholarships and grants from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must have financial need to qualify.
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Need-based self-help aid: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Loans and jobs}{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624  }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 
 from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must demonstrate financial need to qualify.
\par 
\par }{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Non-need-based }{\b\cf1\insrsid1912817\charrsid15034624 scholarship or grant}{\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624  aid: }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Scholarships and grants, gifts, or merit-based ai
d from institutional, state, federal, or other sources (including unrestricted funds or gifts and endowment income) awarded solely on the basis of academic achievement, merit, or any other non-need-based reason. When reporting questions H1 and H2, non-nee
d-based aid that is used to meet need should be counted as need-based aid. 
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid75816 {\b\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Note: Suggested order of precedence for counting non-need money as need-based:
\par }{\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Non-need institutional grants
\par Non-need tuition waivers
\par Non-need athletic awards
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid75816 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cf1\insrsid75816\charrsid15034624 Non-need federal grants
